# SPA fallback (Netlify-style syntax, honored by a number of static hosts).
#
# The build produces exactly one HTML file. Routes like /journey or /leadership
# exist only inside React Router, in the browser — there is no file on disk at
# those paths. Without this rule, refreshing on a sub-route (or opening a shared
# link to one) makes the browser request a path the host can't find: a 404.
#
# "Serve index.html for anything you don't have a real file for, with a 200 so
# it isn't treated as an error page." React Router then resolves the URL client
# side. Real assets under /assets/* still win, since the host matches actual
# files before applying this.
/*    /index.html   200
